Parser provenance
lib/scan-exclusion.cjs and tests/fixtures/parser-vectors.json are adapted from
our author-owned st-loreveil (AGPL-3.0), local reference commit
587e050408882c79841183af44b011aa91763bf6.
Source: lib/scan-exclusion.js and tests/test-vectors.json.
Adaptation: CommonJS, fixed wi-exclude tag/attribute/marker names, exact
/wi[-_]exclude/i fast path, and immutable chat-role message projection.

Marinara test fixtures
Tests contain readable JavaScript transpiled from Pasta-Devs/Marinara-Engine,
licensed AGPL-3.0 by its authors/contributors. Source repository:
https://github.com/Pasta-Devs/Marinara-Engine
v2.5.1: ef069642164c57c8216585b0dde4c5aab1a508fe
v2.5.2: ed8ac0f2c93888aec252116796b865aaa29e1791
Exact paths, build settings and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in
 tests/fixtures/marinara/manifest.json.
Runtime code does not bundle the engine. Test fixture import bindings are
replaced only by the test harness; keyword matching and scanner functions
remain the compiled upstream implementation.
The fix1 fixtures also include the upstream prompt regex application,
replacement helpers, default regex seeding definitions and request logging.

Memory runtime attribution
The load-hook structure (Node module.registerHooks, nextLoad chaining,
source conversion, exact-once source anchors and independent patch logging)
is adapted from tlsiddl/marinara-memory-module
(https://github.com/tlsiddl/marinara-memory-module), commit 8d5f090,
memory-module/marinara-memory-runtime.cjs (runtime version 0.12.6).
The original lists supported versions but does not enforce them; LoreVeil
adds its own package identity/version checks. No unrelated memory service
code is incorporated in this project. Its original runtime is used externally
for coexistence tests. The MIT notice follows in full.

